Yahan teen naye alfaaz ek saath aaye hain, inhein achhi tarah alag alag pehchaan lein:
derivative: woh limit khud, yani \(f'(x)\);
differentiable: jis point par yeh limit maujood ho, wahan function differentiable kehlata hai;
differentiation: derivative nikalne ka amal (process).
Jumlon mein dekhiye: "\(x^{2}\) ka derivative \(2x\) hai", "\(x^{2}\) har \(x\) par differentiable hai", "humne \(x^{2}\) ki differentiation ki". Teeno ek hi khandaan ke lafz hain magar kaam alag alag. Exam mein inhein aapas mein mila dena (mix karna) aam ghalti hai.
